  "reviewedChanges": [
    {
      "sourceLines": "110-129 and133",
      "qualification": "The first comparison accepts the pinned resolved undefined sentinel, followed immediately by a strict array check and zero dependency length. The original explicitly disabled inline configuration input is unchanged. Missing server/config cannot pass both first conditions. No loaded configuration filename or nonempty dependency list is admitted.",
      "sourceEvidence": "The exact saved Vite resolver skips file loading on the explicit disabled input, initializes no dependencies and emits the undefined resolved sentinel. This is source compatibility, not proof of actual context values."
    },
    {
      "sourceLines": "114-126",
      "qualification": "Ten closures are evaluated sequentially and stop on the first comparison which fails or throws. All eight original later comparison expressions are text-identical and in their original order; no later getter is invoked by diagnostic assembly. Completed entries are strict booleans and unevaluated/throwing comparisons keep the fixed not-evaluated marker."
    },
    {
      "sourceLines": "110-111,127",
      "qualification": "The module-private weak association stores only a frozen ten-slot result array keyed by the original thrown object. Fixed condition names are a separate frozen literal list. The new retained data does not store context, configuration, reporter or arbitrary input values. Failure to retain diagnostics is caught and the original thrown value is rethrown unchanged."
    },
    {
      "sourceLines": "154-160",
      "qualification": "The existing private error snapshot adds facts only when it finds exactly ten array entries whose own data descriptors contain one of the three closed result values. Names come from the fixed list, not user data; unreadable diagnostics return no addition. The original public summary expression is byte-identical. Existing bounded private error-byte retention remains unchanged."
    },
    {
      "sourceLines": "222-237 and complete inverse",
      "qualification": "Original primary error, secondary context-close/final-source/report-retention handling and exclusive private driver-report retention remain unchanged. The public return still removes privateFailure. This does not upgrade failed retention, permit a retry, or replace a primary error with a diagnostic or close failure."
    }
  ],
